  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "MOD with operands below about 1E-290 gives wrong signs and #NUM!",
  "statement": "When both operands are below about 1E-290, MOD can return -n itself, or #NUM! at small quotients, where the exact answer is an ordinary number. MOD(-(1+121*2^-52)*2^-983, 2^-983) returns +(1+121*2^-52)*2^-983, and MOD(2^-983, -(1+120*2^-52)*2^-983) returns #NUM!. All 4,974 MOD mismatches in the bank lie in this domain.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Recorded rows of the W111 MOD tiny-operand discrimination run; 147,458 of 152,432 bank rows match without this domain.",
